"imdb_id": "tt0056171",
"original_title": "Ro.Go.Pa.G.",
"overview": "Four short films by four different directors dealing with the principles of modern life. \"Illibatezza\" (Rossellini): The hostess Anna Maria, to dissuade an aggressive suitor who prefers maternal tendencies, assumes an unscrupulous attitude, obeying the suggestions of her distant boyfriend. \"The New World\" (Godard): The deflagration of an atomic bomb causes strange effects on the inhabitants of a city. \"La ricotta\" (Pasolini): During the filming of a film about a religious subject, the extra Stracci dies hanging on the cross due to an indigestion of ricotta. \"Il pollo spante\" (Gregoretti): While an expert illustrates to a board of merchants the most modern techniques to increase sales through the discovery of the secret self of the average consumer, the human story of a bourgeois who, following these suggestions, focuses on the purchase of a plot of land in the countryside.",
"poster": "https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342/AjZgOidGeYN6ZGDHlwx1RZ9UFXV.jpg",
